---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ImagePlaceholder from "../../components/ImagePlaceholder.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import MailButton from "../../components/MailButton.astro";
import poohAtWork from "../../assets/images/illustrations/pooh-at-work.webp";
import { enPerson, enBreadcrumb } from "../../utils/schema-en";
import { EMAIL, EMAIL_URL, GITHUB_URL } from "../../../site.config.mjs";

const personSchema = enPerson(Astro.site);

const aboutPageSchema = {
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "AboutPage",
	name: "About Purin Buriwong",
	url: new URL("/en/about/", Astro.site).href,
	mainEntity: { "@type": "Person", name: "Purin Buriwong" },
};

const breadcrumb = enBreadcrumb(Astro.site, "About", "/en/about/");

const facts: { label: string; value: string }[] = [
	{ label: "Name", value: "Purin Buriwong" },
	{ label: "Goes by", value: "Pooh" },
	{ label: "Role", value: "Business Technology Engineer" },
	{ label: "Based in", value: "Bangkok, Thailand. Works with clients worldwide." },
	{ label: "Languages", value: "Thai and English" },
	{
		label: "Education",
		value: "Computer Engineering, Mahidol University International College",
	},
	{ label: "Experience", value: "More than seven years building software" },
];

const services: { label: string; href: string }[] = [
	{ label: "Business systems and internal software", href: "/en/backoffice/" },
	{ label: "Business websites", href: "/en/work/" },
	{ label: "Repairing sites that AI started", href: "/en/fix-ai-website/" },
	{ label: "What drives the budget", href: "/en/budget-factors/" },
];
---

<Layout
	lang="en"
	title="Purin Buriwong (Pooh), Senior Developer in Bangkok | Pooh"
	description="Purin Buriwong, known as Pooh. Senior software engineer in Bangkok with seven years of experience, ex-Agoda, founder of pawjai.co. Builds business websites and internal systems. Email to talk."
	schema={[personSchema, aboutPageSchema, breadcrumb]}
>
	<section class="page-head band-cream">
		<div class="shell page-head-inner">
			<p class="label">About me</p>
			<h1>Purin Buriwong, and why I still maintain what I ship</h1>
			<p class="lede">
				I was writing software professionally before AI could write code. That
				is not nostalgia, it is the reason I build differently:
				<strong
					>a system is not judged the day it launches. It is judged two years
					later, when someone needs to change it.</strong
				>
			</p>
			{/* The entity paragraph. Self-contained on purpose: quoted alone it
			    still says who he is and how to reach him, and Person.description
			    mirrors it. Full-size body copy, never fine print. */}
			<p class="entity">
				<strong
					>Purin Buriwong, who goes by Pooh, is a senior software engineer in
					Bangkok, Thailand.</strong
				> He has more than seven years of experience, he worked on the developer
				team at Agoda, and he founded and still runs <a
					href="https://pawjai.co"
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener">pawjai.co</a
				>. He builds business websites and internal work systems for owners
				operating in and around Thailand and for remote clients abroad, and he
				maintains what he ships. Reach him by email at {EMAIL}.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="intro">
				<div class="intro-media reveal">
					<div class="photo-frame">
						<ImagePlaceholder
							src={poohAtWork}
							alt="Three dimensional illustration of the Pooh mascot working at a desk"
							label="Pooh mascot at work"
							ratio="4 / 5"
							loading="eager"
							fetchpriority="high"
							sizes="(min-width: 68rem) 22rem, (min-width: 48rem) 36vw, calc(100vw - 2.75rem)"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="intro-text reveal reveal-d1">
					<h2>The short version</h2>
					<p>
						I started writing software when there was no tool to write it for
						you. Everything had to be worked out, tried, and fixed by hand.
						That is a slow way to learn and it teaches you things that have not
						stopped being true.
					</p>
					<p>
						I spent time on the developer team at Agoda. That is where I
						learned what a system needs when a lot of real people depend on it
						and nobody can afford for it to be down.
					</p>
					<p>
						Then I founded pawjai.co, a product I built and still run myself.
						When it breaks at an inconvenient hour, I am the one who gets up.
						That changes how you build. You stop making the choice that is easy
						today and expensive in a year, because you are the one who pays for
						it.
					</p>
					<p>
						I use AI every day now, the way any working engineer does. It is
						fast and it is useful.
						<strong
							>The value was never in the tool. It is in knowing which parts
							you can let it handle and which parts will hurt you later.</strong
						>
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section band-tint">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-head reveal">
				<p class="label">Working with me from abroad</p>
				<h2>What it is actually like to hire an engineer here</h2>
			</div>

			<div class="why reveal reveal-d1">
				<p>
					The honest answer to "is this a compromise?" is no. Serious
					engineering has been done in this region for a long time, and the
					reason is simply that the engineers are here. I spent part of my
					career inside one of those teams.
				</p>
				<p>
					What you get by hiring me directly is that more of your budget
					becomes software. There is no agency layer, no account manager
					translating your words into a ticket, and no Western office overhead
					baked into the rate. You talk to the person building the thing.
				</p>
				<p>
					Time zones are the question everyone asks. Bangkok overlaps a
					working morning in Europe and a working evening in Australia. For
					the Americas we agree a fixed window and hold it. In practice the
					thing that decides whether remote work succeeds is not the clock, it
					is whether the scope is written down and you can see progress. Both
					of those are things I do anyway.
				</p>
				<p>
					I also work in Thai. If you are a foreign owner running something
					here, that matters more than it sounds: I can build you an owner's
					view in English and a staff view in Thai out of one system, and you
					are not stuck relying on someone to translate between you and your
					own software.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section">
		<div class="shell">
			<div class="section-head reveal">
				<p class="label">The facts</p>
				<h2>Everything on one page</h2>
			</div>

			<dl class="facts reveal">
				{
					facts.map((f) => (
						<div class="fact">
							<dt>{f.label}</dt>
							<dd>{f.value}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>

			<div class="services reveal reveal-d1">
				<h3>What I take on</h3>
				<ul>
					{
						services.map((sv) => (
							<li>
								<a href={sv.href}>{sv.label}</a>
							</li>
						))
					}
				</ul>
			</div>

			<div class="channels reveal reveal-d2">
				<h3>How to reach me</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						Email <a href={EMAIL_URL}>{EMAIL}</a>. I read and answer every one
						myself.
					</li>
					<li>
						If you are already in Thailand and prefer a chat app, that option
						is on the <a href="/en/contact/">contact page</a>.
					</li>
					<li>
						Code samples are on <a href={GITHUB_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
							>GitHub</a
						>.
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="band">
		<div class="shell band-inner reveal">
			<p class="label">Get in touch</p>
			<h2>Want to know whether I can help? Ask me.</h2>
			<p class="lede">
				Tell me what your business does and what is getting in the way. I will
				tell you where I would start, and if I am not the right person I will
				say that too.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<MailButton label={`Email ${EMAIL}`} tone="on-dark" />
				<a class="cta-quiet" href="/en/work/">
					See the work
					<Icon name="arrow" size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</Layout>

<style>
	.entity {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		max-width: 38rem;
		color: var(--ink);
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
	}

	.page-head .lede strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	.intro {
		display: grid;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.intro-media,
	.intro-text {
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.photo-frame {
		position: relative;
		max-width: 20rem;
	}

	.photo-frame::before {
		content: "";
		position: absolute;
		inset: 0;
		transform: translate(0.75rem, 0.75rem);
		border: 1.5px solid var(--honey);
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		opacity: 0.4;
		pointer-events: none;
	}

	.photo-frame :global(.ph) {
		position: relative;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		overflow: hidden;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	.intro-text {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		align-content: center;
	}

	.intro-text h2 {
		font-size: var(--fs-h2);
	}

	.intro-text p {
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 38rem;
	}

	.intro-text strong {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-weight: 500;
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.intro {
			grid-template-columns: 0.8fr 1.2fr;
			gap: 3rem;
			align-items: center;
		}
	}

	.why {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
	}

	.why p {
		color: var(--muted);
		max-width: 38rem;
	}

	.facts {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0;
		margin: 0;
		border-radius: var(--radius);
		background: var(--paper);
		border: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm);
		overflow: hidden;
	}

	.fact {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.125rem 1.5rem;
		padding: 0.875rem 1.25rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
		min-width: 0;
	}

	.fact:first-child {
		border-top: 0;
	}

	.facts dt {
		font-family: var(--font-head);
		font-weight: 500;
		font-size: var(--fs-label);
		color: var(--honey-ink);
	}

	.facts dd {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
		min-width: 0;
	}

	@media (min-width: 48em) {
		.fact {
			grid-template-columns: 10rem minmax(0, 1fr);
			align-items: baseline;
			padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
		}
	}

	.services,
	.channels {
		margin-top: 2rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.625rem;
	}

	.services h3,
	.channels h3 {
		font-size: var(--fs-body);
		font-weight: 600;
	}

	.services ul,
	.channels ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.4375rem;
	}

	.services li,
	.channels li {
		font-size: var(--fs-body-sm);
		color: var(--muted);
		min-width: 0;
	}
</style>
